{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1777734513989,"sessionID":"ses_216c60402ffe2JsfyY5wEgPCMY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"toolu_bdrk_01GNRZWHFAqfg2MDi2r4bfYg","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/work/push_swap.rs","newString":"// Sort 3 elements on top of a (a.len() == 3 here).\nfn sort3(ps: &mut Ps) {\n    let a = ps.a_top();\n    let b = ps.a_second();\n    let c = ps.a_third();\n    // Compute local ranks among {a,b,c}.\n    let r0 = (if b < a { 1 } else { 0 }) + (if c < a { 1 } else { 0 });\n    let r1 = (if a < b { 1 } else { 0 }) + (if c < b { 1 } else { 0 });\n    let r2 = (if a < c { 1 } else { 0 }) + (if b < c { 1 } else { 0 });\n    // Stack top..bot corresponds to (r0, r1, r2). We want (0, 1, 2).\n    // (0,1,2): noop\n    // (0,2,1): rra; sa\n    // (1,0,2): sa\n    // (1,2,0): rra\n    // (2,0,1): ra\n    // (2,1,0): sa; rra\n    if r0 == 0 && r1 == 1 && r2 == 2 {\n        // noop\n    } else if r0 == 0 && r1 == 2 && r2 == 1 {\n        ps.rra();\n        ps.sa();\n    } else if r0 == 1 && r1 == 0 && r2 == 2 {\n        ps.sa();\n    } else if r0 == 1 && r1 == 2 && r2 == 0 {\n        ps.rra();\n    } else if r0 == 2 && r1 == 0 && r2 == 1 {\n        ps.ra();\n    } else {\n        // (2,1,0)\n        ps.sa();\n        ps.rra();\n    }\n}","oldString":"// Sort 3 elements on top of a (entire a has exactly 3 elements here, or at\n// least we're sorting a.len() == 3 using only ra/rra/sa).\nfn sort3(ps: &mut Ps) {\n    // a values (top to bottom): x, y, z where top = last in vec.\n    let top = ps.a_top();\n    let mid = ps.a_second();\n    let bot = ps.a_third();\n    // We want ascending smallest on top => top < mid < bot.\n    // Permutation cases:\n    if top < mid && mid < bot {\n        // already sorted\n    } else if top < mid && mid > bot && top < bot {\n        // top, mid, bot = 1, 3, 2 → sa then rra? Let's enumerate cleanly.\n        // Easiest: enumerate the 6 permutations by rank.\n        unreachable!()\n    } else {\n        // fallthrough; handled below\n    }\n    // Use a straightforward case table on the ranks of the 3 elements.\n    // Compute local ranks.\n    let a = top;\n    let b = mid;\n    let c = bot;\n    // r0 = rank of top, r1 = rank of mid, r2 = rank of bot among {a,b,c}\n    let r0 = (if b < a { 1 } else { 0 }) + (if c < a { 1 } else { 0 });\n    let r1 = (if a < b { 1 } else { 0 }) + (if c < b { 1 } else { 0 });\n    let r2 = (if a < c { 1 } else { 0 }) + (if b < c { 1 } else { 0 });\n    // Permutation (r0,r1,r2):\n    // (0,1,2): sorted, noop\n    // (0,2,1): sa; rra ??  Wait: top=0,mid=2,bot=1. We need 0,1,2.\n    //   rra moves bot to top → stack becomes 1,0,2. Then sa → 0,1,2. (2 ops)\n    // (1,0,2): sa (swap top two) → 0,1,2. (1 op)\n    // (1,2,0): ra → bot=1 comes under; sequence: top=1,mid=2,bot=0\n    //   ra moves top to bottom → stack (top→bot): 2,0,1. not right.\n    //   Best: rra → 0,1,2. (1 op)\n    // (2,0,1): top=2,mid=0,bot=1; ra → 0,1,2 (1 op)\n    // (2,1,0): top=2,mid=1,bot=0; sa → 1,2,0; rra → 0,1,2. (2 ops)\n    if r0 == 0 && r1 == 1 && r2 == 2 {\n        // noop\n    } else if r0 == 0 && r1 == 2 && r2 == 1 {\n        ps.rra();\n        ps.sa();\n    } else if r0 == 1 && r1 == 0 && r2 == 2 {\n        ps.sa();\n    } else if r0 == 1 && r1 == 2 && r2 == 0 {\n        ps.rra();\n    } else if r0 == 2 && r1 == 0 && r2 == 1 {\n        ps.ra();\n    } else {\n        // (2,1,0)\n        ps.sa();\n        ps.rra();\n    }\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /work/push_swap.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /work/push_swap.rs\n+++ /work/push_swap.rs\n@@ -324,45 +324,24 @@\n // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n // Small-n sorters\n // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n-// Sort 3 elements on top of a (entire a has exactly 3 elements here, or at\n-// least we're so