{"type":"text","timestamp":1777734684686,"sessionID":"ses_216c60402ffe2JsfyY5wEgPCMY","part":{"id":"prt_de93e849a0011WjmYIY3OX2CN9","messageID":"msg_de93e80e8001I18k7jWXL4LrXa","sessionID":"ses_216c60402ffe2JsfyY5wEgPCMY","type":"text","text":"Good. Now let me also update the Makefile's `clean` — traditionally `clean` removes object files (in C, `.o`), and `fclean` removes those plus the binary. For Rust here, there are effectively no intermediate files (other than any `.d` dep file, which rustc doesn't always produce). The Makefile is fine.\n\nLet me do a final check and finalize:","time":{"start":1777734681754,"end":1777734684685}}}
